          "filename": "110727-N-XD935-231 (5988128648).jpg",
          "caption": "Jamaica Defense Force Coast Guard Lt. j.g. Christopher YeeSing, left, a diving officer, gives the okay signal during his descent to retrieve an underwater salvage project on the sea floor as part of a joint diving salvage operation with Mobile Diving and Salvage Unit (MDSU) 2 in Port Royal, Jamaica, July 27, 2011. MDSU-2 was participating in Navy Diver-Southern Partnership Station, an annual deployment of U.S. ships to the U.S. Southern Command's area of responsibility in the Caribbean and Latin America. The exercise involves information sharing with navies, coast guards and civilian services throughout the region. (DoD photo by Mass Communication Specialist 1st Class Jayme Pastoric, U.S. Navy/Released)",
